# ==== T-FMT-B — SYNONYM: prefix `await` at an OWNERSHIP-MODIFIER operand
# position (brief-review pass 6).
# SCOPE CLAIM: the second form-dependent predicate,
# `emits_leading_ownership_sigil`. At a call-argument / for-iterable position
# the parser strips a leading `&` / `!` / `^` into the enclosing node's
# ownership field BEFORE the expression parser runs, so the formatter wraps any
# expression whose emission STARTS with a sigil. For `Expr::Await` that
# predicate recurses into the RECEIVER — correct for the postfix rendering
# (`^x.m().await()` leads with `^`) and WRONG for the prefix rendering, whose
# leftmost token is the `await` keyword. A prefix await must gain no parens.
async int f():
    return 1

void consume(int x):
    print(x)

async void g():
    consume(await f())

async void main():
    await g()
